    <string name="match_help_title">How to Play Matching</string>
    <string name="match_help_text">Find all the pairs.

The cards lie face down. On your turn, turn over two cards. If the pictures are the same, you keep the pair and go again. If not, they turn back over and the next player goes.

The board ends when every pair is found. With several players, the most pairs wins. Playing alone, try to finish in as few moves and as little time as you can: Hint and Undo are there to help, but a run that uses them is not saved as a personal best.

The menu lets you change the pictures: friendly critters, bold symbols or playing cards.</string>
